The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table, the
desk's view below, says otherwise. Read report by report, against each reporter's tenant, the
ticket holds three problems. #4471 is the parser problem, and its queued fix only reaches that one.
The other two have no ticket of their own, so they get one here.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The queued parser fix leaves the form hint and the one-day moves open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## A ticket for each problem

| problem | what goes wrong | reports | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | The shared parser reads a day-first date month first: day and month swap. | the `parser` row | #4471 itself, fix queued |
| `hint` | booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field; people type month first and the form reads it day first. | the `hint` row | [#2](https://github.com/CamiloGaete/support-kb-4471/issues/2) |
| one-day | The date lands one day early or late, not on a swapped month. | the one-day reads in the footnote | [#7](https://github.com/CamiloGaete/support-kb-4471/issues/7) |

Parser keeps #4471. The two new tickets list their report ids and their counts.

## How each report was placed

1. One report per id. The ticket system exports in overlapping pages, so some reports come twice.
2. The desk's one-day notes go first. A report that says the date moved by one day did not get a
   flipped month, whatever its tenant.
3. Every other report goes by its tenant and the way it came in, as
   [`causes.ts`](https://github.com/CamiloGaete/support-kb-4471/blob/main/support-kb/src/lib/kb/causes.ts)
   runs it: a form report from a day-first tenant on booking-v3 is `hint`, the rest is `parser`.
4. Intake's tag is not used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser, and the table's "tagged
   as" column shows how often it names the other cause.

Every body was read. Apart from the one-day reads, each report under `parser` or `hint` either
swaps day and month, or gives no date to check against.

## What changes for the desk

- **parser** is what #4471 already describes, and its queued fix stays the right fix for these
  reports.
- **hint** survives that fix. booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, so
  people at day-first tenants type the month first, and the form reads their input day first.
  The form needs the tenant's own order under its date field, as booking-v2 already does.
- **one-day** is a third bug: the date lands a day early or late, and one report has the same
  meeting on different days in Lisbon and Toronto. Look at how the date crosses time zones on
  its way into the invite.
- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, so reports with
  the same subject and different causes ended up in one ticket. A new decision record should
  replace 0001; this page does not edit it.

